meta {
  name: Add to cart
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shop/cart/lines
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{shopToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "variantId": 1,
    "quantity": 2
  }
}

docs {
  Notice what you **cannot** send: a price. A cart that accepted one from the browser would let
  the browser set it. The price comes from Pricing, live, on every cart operation — an
  architecture test fails the build if a money-shaped field ever appears on a shop request.

  The response includes `changes`: anything repriced or removed since you last looked. It is
  part of the cart, not an error channel, and a client that ignores it still shows the right
  total.
}
